  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Media Between Text\n\nA sentence with a gap in the middle: a rounded media tile springs open between the two halves, pushing the words apart, then closes again. The tile is a drawn gradient by default, or your own image.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 4.5 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A line of text should open a gap and show a picture, clip or swatch inline, as part of the sentence.\n- A headline needs an image tucked between its words, appearing with a spring.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The picture should fill the frame or sit in a separate layout: use a scene or panel block.\n- The text must not shift while the media appears.\n\nVariables:\n- first_text (string): First text, default \"that's a nice (\"\n- second_text (string): Second text, default \") chair!\"\n- font_size (number, 24-260): Font size, default 96\n- font_weight (enum): Font weight, default \"300\"\n- color (color): Text color, default \"#e11d48\"\n- media_width (number, 0.3-4): Media width, default 1.7\n- media_height (number, 0.3-4): Media height, default 1.7\n- media_radius (number, 0-1): Media radius, default 0.12\n- gradient_from (color): Gradient from, default \"#fda4af\"\n- gradient_to (color): Gradient to, default \"#6d28d9\"\n- image (string): Image, default \"\"\n- open_at (number, 0-3): Open at, default 0.5\n- close_at (number, 0-8): Close at, default 3.2\n- spring_duration (number, 0.1-2): Spring duration, default 0.4\n\nSource: https://github.com/danielpetho/fancy. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
